{#
    A band: the ground runs edge to edge, the content does not.

    `.sds-bands` on the page draws the hairline between two of them and makes
    consecutive bands share one line rather than each drawing its own. The
    quiet variant is the second ground — what makes a run of bands read as
    alternating instead of as a wall.

    The document's nodes stand in the band itself. A box between the two takes
    the band's own rule off them — the last block's step is given up at the
    edge of the band, and a wrapper in between kept it, so every band was one
    step deeper below its content than above it. The heading is plain: the
    document layer is what sets a heading, and a class here would be the one
    `h2` on the page ignoring it.
#}
<section class="sds-band{% if node.option('quiet') %} sds-band--quiet{% endif %}"
         {%- if node.option('id') %} id="{{ node.option('id') }}"{% endif %}>
    {%- if node.option('title') %}
        <h2>{{ node.option('title') }}</h2>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- for child in node.children -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</section>
